  "content": {
    "id": "p76-q10-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "10",
    "prompt": "Tom is designing a card game. His deck must be able to be divided evenly between 2 to 6 players. What is the smallest number of cards that his deck could have?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "60 cards.",
      "worked": "The number of cards must be a multiple of each of $2,3,4,5,6$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}2&=2^1\\times3^0\\times5^0\\\\3&=2^0\\times3^1\\times5^0\\\\4&=2^2\\times3^0\\times5^0\\\\5&=2^0\\times3^0\\times5^1\\\\6&=2^1\\times3^1\\times5^0\\end{align*}$$\n\nChoose the largest power of each prime factor.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\operatorname{LCM}(2,3,4,5,6)&=2^2\\times3\\times5\\\\\\operatorname{LCM}(2,3,4,5,6)&=60\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe smallest deck has 60 cards.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 50
  },
